[ac-13]\n    Given: session ends\n    When: loop completes or errors\n    Then: logs session.end event with status and triggers commit\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: a loop iteration starts\n    When: building prompt for the agent\n    Then: creates a fresh ACP session so each iteration has a clean context window\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: --focus flag is provided with instructions\n    When: building prompt for each iteration\n    Then: includes the focus instructions prominently in the prompt, emphasizing they apply to all iterations\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: ralph loop is running\n    When: checking for available tasks (ready or in_progress)\n    Then: only considers tasks with automation: eligible status; both ready tasks and in_progress tasks are filtered by automation eligibility\n  [ac-17]\n    Given: ralph loop is running with --restart-every N (N > 0)\n    When: iteration completes and iteration number is divisible by N\n    Then: agent process is killed and respawned to prevent memory buildup\n  [ac-18]\n    Given: --restart-every 0 is specified\n    When: iterations complete\n    Then: agent process is never restarted (maintains single agent instance)\n  [ac-19]\n    Given: ralph loop iteration completes\n    When: determining whether to continue looping\n    Then: loop continues if automation:eligible ready tasks OR automation:eligible in_progress tasks exist; exits with message when neither remain\n  [ac-20]\n    Given: processPendingReviewTasks completes during iteration\n    When: checking for loop continuation\n    Then: uses freshly gathered task context (not stale from iteration start) to detect tasks that became ready due to dependency unblocking\n  [ac-21]\n    Given: User runs kspec ralph with --tasks @ref1,@ref2\n    When: task selection runs each iteration\n    Then: only the explicitly listed tasks are considered for work, regardless of automation eligibility of other tasks; exits when all listed tasks are completed or blocked\n  [ac-22]\n    Given: A terminal/run tool request produces large stdout or stderr output\n    When: Ralph handles the terminal/run request\n    Then: Ralph streams stdout and stderr to per-session artifact files under .kspec/sessions/{session}/tool-output/ instead of accumulating unbounded output in memory\n  [ac-23]\n    Given: A terminal/run command completes after producing output\n    When: Ralph sends the tool response and renders tool output\n    Then: The response includes bounded previews and metadata (stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated) while preserving access to full output via artifact files\n  [ac-24]\n    Given: --iteration-timeout <minutes> is provided (default: 20)\n    When: ralph runs an iteration\n    Then: the entire task-work and reflect prompt phase is bounded by that timeout; defaults to 20 minutes if not specified\n  [ac-25]\n    Given: --iteration-timeout receives a non-positive or non-numeric value\n    When: ralph starts\n    Then: exits immediately with an error indicating --iteration-timeout must be a positive number of minutes\n  [ac-26]\n    Given: an iteration timeout fires while agent is still running\n    When: the timeout expires\n    Then: logs iteration.timeout event with iteration/attempt/timeout metadata and applies existing retry/failure escalation logic\n\nRemember: Add test coverage for each AC and mark tests with // AC: @spec-ref ac-N\n\n","status":"completed"}